      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Maximum likelihood provides for extremely convenient tests of hypotheses in the form of likelihood-ratio, or LR, tests (reviewed in Chapter 24 of Kendall and Stuart 1979) that examine whether a reduced model provides the same fit as a full model. The likelihood-ratio test statistic is given by",
